.TH NOTEPAD-PLUS-PLUS-GTK 1 "October 2026" "Notepad++ GTK port" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
notepad-plus-plus-gtk \- Notepad++ source code editor, native GTK 3 port (preview)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B notepad-plus-plus-gtk
[\fB\-n\fIline\fR] [\fB\-c\fIcolumn\fR] [\fB\-l\fIlanguage\fR] [\fB\-ro\fR] [\fB\-multiInst\fR] [\fB\-nosession\fR] [\fIfile\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B notepad-plus-plus-gtk
is an unofficial native Linux build of the Notepad++ source tree. It uses the
GTK 3 backend of Scintilla, the Lexilla lexers, and the language, style and
theme definitions shipped with Notepad++.
.PP
Files given on the command line are opened in tabs. A file that does not
exist yet is opened empty and created on first save.
.PP
Only one instance runs per user session: when the editor is already running,
the files and switches are handed to it over D-Bus and the command returns at
once. On start the previous session is restored, including unsaved documents
kept by the periodic snapshot (Settings > Preferences > Backup).
.SH OPTIONS
Switches follow the Notepad++ command line syntax.
.TP
.BI \-n line
Move the caret to \fIline\fR (1-based) in the opened files.
.TP
.BI \-c column
Move the caret to \fIcolumn\fR (1-based).
.TP
.BI \-l language
Apply \fIlanguage\fR instead of detecting it from the file name, for example
\fB\-lpython\fR or \fB\-l"C++"\fR.
.TP
.B \-ro
Open the files read-only.
.TP
.B \-multiInst
Start a separate instance instead of using the running one. As in Notepad++,
an additional instance neither restores nor saves the session.
.TP
.B \-nosession
Do not restore the previous session at start or save it at exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-exit\-after= ms
Quit after \fIms\fR milliseconds (used by automated smoke tests).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.PP
\fB\-notabbar\fR, \fB\-nosys\fR and \fB\-noPlugin\fR are accepted for
compatibility and ignored.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/notepad-plus-plus-gtk/settings.ini
Settings, window geometry and the recent files list.
.TP
.I ~/.config/notepad-plus-plus-gtk/session.xml
The last session, in the Notepad++ format. The previous copy is kept as
\fIsession.xml.inCaseOfCorruption.bak\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/notepad-plus-plus-gtk/backup/
Snapshots of unsaved documents, named \fIname\fR@\fItimestamp\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/notepad-plus-plus-gtk/config.xml
A Notepad++ configuration copied from Windows. Its settings (session and
backup options, tab settings, theme, recent files and others) are imported
on first start; Settings > Import Notepad++ config.xml imports one later.
.TP
.I ~/.config/notepad-plus-plus-gtk/langs.xml
.TQ
.I ~/.config/notepad-plus-plus-gtk/stylers.xml
Optional user overrides of the shipped language and style definitions
(same format as Notepad++ on Windows). The Style Configurator saves to
\fIstylers.xml\fR, or to a copy of the chosen theme in \fIthemes/\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/notepad-plus-plus-gtk/shortcuts.xml
Changed keyboard shortcuts, saved macros and Run commands, in the Notepad++
format; a file from Notepad++ on Windows works as it is.
.TP
.I ~/.config/notepad-plus-plus-gtk/userDefineLang.xml
.TQ
.I ~/.config/notepad-plus-plus-gtk/userDefineLangs/
User Defined Languages in the Notepad++ format.
.TP
.I ~/.config/notepad-plus-plus-gtk/themes/
Additional Notepad++ theme files.
.TP
.I /usr/share/notepad-plus-plus-gtk/
Shipped language, style and theme definitions.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NPP_GTK_DATA_DIR
Overrides the directory holding the shipped definitions.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://notepad-plus-plus.org/
